# RETIRED SCAFFOLD SOURCE (SN-028). This dial now lives in
# process.toml.template -> docs/process.toml as `[policies] push`, and
# bootstrap.py no longer copies this file into a new repo — shipping both
# homes would hand every scaffold the mixed-config refusal. The file stays
# in the kit as the reference for the legacy vocabulary that
# `bootstrap.py --migrate-config` reads when converting an existing
# adoption; the text below describes that legacy home, not today's.
#
# Push policy (process.md §7; process-options.md "Agent iteration branch &
# sync"). One value on the last line — who may publish (`git push`) this repo:
#   human           — the default: an agent never pushes, even if asked
#                     mid-session; it prepares the branch and requests a push.
#   agent-iteration — an agent may push only the scrubbed llm/<branch>
#                     iteration branch; the development branch stays
#                     human-pushed.
#   agent           — an agent may push the development branch after a landed
#                     sync (full delegation, still gated by the sync ritual).
# A process rule honored by agent drivers and coordinators (hooks are
# per-clone and can only assist). Change this value in a reviewed commit,
# like the other declared policy files.
human
